Subject: [PATCH] 5446 (D792), second half: a solved case finds its helper
 through a contact too

0387 made a solved goal find its helper among the asker's own contacts.
5446's DONE WHEN also has owner C, who holds the helper only through one of
C's contacts. search_second_degree now reads helper_solved_cases for the
people the asker's bridges hold, matched on the goal's words.

A person found that way and no other carries from_case. They are given the
approved BP note (found_by_their_own_work: offer them, never say why) and no
employer or role, the same rule search_by_tag already applies. Someone also
found by a label or fact is shown as before.

Run against Postgres 16 with the live column types: the generated query
finds the helper through the bridge with case_only true, and false once a
bridge's tag also matches.

